{
	"_note": "Adventures: everything pets are sent out to do. TYPES group locations and unlock over time ('unlocked': true = from the start; 'unlock': { 'after_trips': n } = after n trips welcomed back; 'unlock': 'rumour' = when a rumour leads there). LOCATIONS are chains of events: a fixed 'events' list, or a weighted 'pool' that each trip draws 'draws' events from without repeats; 'go_home': true adds a 'go home' option (keep the bag) to every event there ('locked': true = only once a rumour leads there; 'unlock': { 'after_trips': n } = after n trips welcomed back; otherwise open whenever their type is): 'minutes' is the whole trip (events spread evenly, then the walk home), 'max_party' 0 = as many as you may send, 'difficulty' multiplies option difficulty, 'danger' multiplies how many get hurt or lost, 'loot' multiplies coins, 'box' is the box found there and the odds for part rarity. EVENTS are shared. Option: 'stat' is tested against 'difficulty' with the party's total (empty = always works), 'tag' is for policies, 'min_party' hides it for smaller parties. Option 'chance': its own chance of going well (tilted a little by 'stat' and down if hurt); no chance and no stat = always works. Outcome: 'lost'/'injured'/'heal' are [min, max] fractions of the party, 'hurt' is a fraction of pets that lose a heart ('hearts': 2 = both at once; a pet hurt twice doesn't come back, and nothing it found comes home), 'progress' is continue / end / skip, 'leave_injured' leaves the injured behind, 'rewards' is a list of { kind, ... } handled in scripts/adventure/rewards.gd (coins: 'amount' per pet; box/part/rumour/anything else: 'chance', growing with the square root of the party). RUMOURS are what exploration brings back: 'about' is how the pet describes it, 'unlocks' what saying yes opens, 'requires' what must be open before anyone can hear it. {who} is the pet's name, or 'the party'. Texts stay cheerful and plain.",
